<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crimean Tatars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Crimean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> are a Turkic Muslim people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimean peninsula</a>. They formed the core of the Crimean Khanate, an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> annexed Crimea in 1783, after which many emigrated to Ottoman lands. In 1917 they proclaimed the short-lived Crimean People's Republic, and in 1944 Stalin deported the entire people to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crimean-tatars.jpg" alt="Crimean Tatars" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Riwnodennyk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Crimean_Tatar_people.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
